Project Workflow


Create the Azure Environment
Create a resource group, virtual network (VNet), subnet, network security group (NSG), and deploy a Windows virtual machine (VM) in Microsoft Azure.


Configure Network Access
Configure NSG inbound rules to allow RDP traffic to the VM. Verify that the VM is reachable from the public internet by testing connectivity.


Install and Configure the Azure Monitor Agent
Install the Azure Monitor Agent (AMA) on the VM and connect the VM to a Log Analytics Workspace.


Create a Data Collection Rule
Configure a Data Collection Rule (DCR) to collect Windows security event logs and other relevant telemetry.


Enable Microsoft Sentinel
Enable Microsoft Sentinel on the Log Analytics Workspace and verify that logs from the VM are being ingested successfully.


Add GeoIP Enrichment
Create a watchlist using a pre-built GeoIP dataset to enrich incoming security logs with geographic information.


Analyze Logs with KQL
Use Kusto Query Language (KQL) to query security events and correlate IP addresses with GeoIP data to identify the source locations of login attempts.
let GeoIPDB_FULL = _GetWatchlist("geoip");
let WindowsEvents = SecurityEvent
    | where IpAddress == <attacker IP address>
    | where EventID == 4625
    | order by TimeGenerated desc
    | evaluate ipv4_lookup(GeoIPDB_FULL, IpAddress, network);
WindowsEvents



Build a Workbook Visualization
Create a Microsoft Sentinel workbook and paste the map visualization query to display attack sources on a geographic map.


Generate and Investigate Events
Generate authentication activity against the VM and observe the resulting security events, failed logons, and geographic distribution of connection attempts in Sentinel.


Review Findings
Review the collected logs, validate that logs are flowing correctly, and document observations. 


